{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"2b1abf81a25d731a","type":"group","x":-700,"y":-840,"width":1020,"height":740,"color":"1","label":"Actions"},
		{"id":"a93701e883ee6b61","type":"group","x":340,"y":-840,"width":860,"height":560,"color":"2","label":"Reactions"},
		{"id":"184cfb9a9a66741a","type":"group","x":340,"y":-220,"width":900,"height":460,"color":"3","label":"Free Action"},
		{"id":"28c173aa045be2c5","type":"text","text":"# Attack\n1. Roll skill dice to determine success\n2. The opponent may parry or evade\n3. If attack connects then use specials if avalible\n4. Roll hit location die (d20)\n5. Roll damage die. The final damage is the damage rolled - opponents armor.","x":-680,"y":-820,"width":546,"height":260},
		{"id":"ff8943e14980f4eb","type":"text","text":"# Delay\nCharacter can save AP to use as reactions. \nThe AP is expended only after the reaction occurs.\nIf no reactions happen and it's now the players turn in the next round, the AP is essentially lost.","x":-680,"y":-540,"width":546,"height":240},
		{"id":"1131636550d27b87","type":"text","text":"# Regain footing\nAfter getting knocked prone the character can stand up.","x":-100,"y":-440,"width":391,"height":130},
		{"id":"78c6aa92bb05f742","type":"text","text":"# Move\nPlayer can move up to 5 meters + speed modifier (Agility)","x":-100,"y":-820,"width":391,"height":130},
		{"id":"83b6e9870e25cb6f","type":"text","text":"# Reload\nAfter attacking with a ranged weapon the player will have to reload their weapon to be able to shoot again.","x":-100,"y":-652,"width":391,"height":185},
		{"id":"fc27303d681ceb1f","type":"text","text":"# Struggle\nIf the character is grappled, pinned down entangeled he can throw a skill check against the original attackers roll","x":-680,"y":-280,"width":490,"height":160},
		{"id":"baa54ea7bb69721e","type":"text","text":"# Take cover\nThe character can take cover to reduce the chance of being hit provided there is cover avalible.","x":-127,"y":-280,"width":418,"height":159},
		{"id":"7e0f31822305f53c","type":"text","text":"# Evade\nCharacter can use their skill dice (acrobatics) to evade from an attack.\nThis leaves the character prone on the ground.\nThe character has to use the Regain footing action to get back on their feet.\n","x":360,"y":-815,"width":820,"height":163},
		{"id":"f3a3418e21f8b517","type":"text","text":"# Interrupt\nOnly avalible when the player declares the Delay action in their turn.\nThe player can:\n- interrupt enemies action by moving away (opposed roll)\n- make an attack of opportunity\n- ready a shield\n- etc...","x":360,"y":-629,"width":465,"height":319},
		{"id":"352fa979911cea2d","type":"text","text":"# Parry\nThe character can attempt to defend against an incoming attack using a combination of parrying, leaning, ducking, and sidestepping footwork to minimise the blow.","x":840,"y":-629,"width":340,"height":289},
		{"id":"f40cf65da28f765a","type":"text","text":"# Drop item\nDrop an item to the ground.","x":360,"y":-200,"width":360,"height":106},
		{"id":"b229edcd822eb41b","type":"text","text":"# Signal\nSignal by hand to others.","x":360,"y":-80,"width":360,"height":106},
		{"id":"842cfdc416687e57","type":"text","text":"# Speak\nCharacters can speak any time during combat but what is said is limited to short phrases.","x":360,"y":40,"width":360,"height":182},
		{"id":"459b14b503ed2e3c","type":"text","text":"# Ward location\nThe character guards a particular Hit Location from being hit by dedicating one of his weapons to passively block the area. Any blow which lands on that location has its damage automatically downgraded as per normal for a parrying weapon of its Size. The cover continues until the dedicated weapon is used to attack or actively Parry. Establishing or changing the Hit Location covered must be performed prior to an opponent rolling to attack the character. Due to their design, shields can cover multiple areas. Warding weapon/shield can not be used for active parrying.","x":740,"y":-200,"width":480,"height":422},
		{"id":"a1813768b9d644f2","type":"text","text":"# Skills\n\n| Skill LVL | d   | d   | d   | d   | d   |\n| --------- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1         | d6  | d6  | d6  | d6  | d6  |\n| 2         | d8  | d6  | d6  | d6  | d6  |\n| 3         | d8  | d8  | d6  | d6  | d6  |\n| 4         | d8  | d8  | d8  | d6  | d6  |\n| 5         | d8  | d8  | d8  | d8  | d6  |\n| 6         | d8  | d8  | d8  | d8  | d8  |\n| 7         | d10 | d8  | d8  | d8  | d8  |\n| 8         | d10 | d10 | d8  | d8  | d8  |\n| 9         | d10 | d10 | d10 | d8  | d8  |\n| 10        | d10 | d10 | d10 | d10 | d8  |\n| 11        | d10 | d10 | d10 | d10 | d10 |\n| 12        | d12 | d10 | d10 | d10 | d10 |\n| 13        | d12 | d12 | d10 | d10 | d10 |\n| 14        | d12 | d12 | d12 | d10 | d10 |\n| 15        | d12 | d12 | d12 | d12 | d10 |\n| 16        | d12 | d12 | d12 | d12 | d12 |\n# Successes\n\nIf a die roll is higher than 5 it counts as a success.\n\n| Fumbel | Fail | Success | Critical |\n| ------ | ---- | ------- | -------- |\n| 0      | 1-2  | 3-4     | 5        |\nDepending on the difficulty of the task the threshold can move about. Example above is the normal difficulty.\n\nEasy:\n\n| Fumbel | Fail | Success | Critical |\n| ------ | ---- | ------- | -------- |\n| 0      | 1    | 2-4     | 5        |\n\nHard:\n\n| Fumbel | Fail | Success | Critical |\n| ------ | ---- | ------- | -------- |\n| 0      | 1-3  | 4       | 5        |","x":1320,"y":-830,"width":449,"height":1260}
	],
	"edges":[]
}